A||N||6||mope||-= So what if my trunk is rusted through!  Easy fix??||||1||
Z||000000||mope||02-25-2001||08:59 PM||||so my trunk is rusted out, what should i do about repair? I was thinking about just getting a sawsall, cutting out anything rusted then fabricationg myself a new piece of the rusted trunk.<P>I discovered it when taking all the plastic from inside my wheel wells out to clean when i started to poke around and i poked rite into my trunk. oops. i didnt mean to, i just wanted to scrape off the chunky rust. i havent taken out the trunk carpet yet to see how bad it was from the inside yet im gunna do that next week. (only work on the car on saturdays) How much rust damage should i expect to see once i take out the trunk carpet? the car has 71000 miles on it and this is the worst rust ive found on the car. is it worth doing all that cutting and welding or should i just use duct tape and body shutz? Lemme know what you all sugguest.<P>thanks<P>m0pe<P>------------------<BR>=======================<P>-= Silver 86 GT, being restored, and following major things to be done: Mr. Mike's Leather, new steering wheel, paint repair, ebrake repair, take apart and clean everything! <A HREF="http://www.mastergraphics.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mope.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mope.cjb.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-25-2001||09:29 PM||||Definatly get rid of the old rust, sawzall method works great!  You'll probably find more rust on the inside one you remove the carpet.  But if you dont remove all the old rust, and patch it up just so things dont fall through, the rest of the good metal will turn to rust and then you will have no trunk at all.  You must get rid of all the old stuff.  Definatly bend your own sheet metal to repair this.  Are you going to be welding this new piece of metal, or pop-riveting?  Either way, I would suggest not trying to make the new bottom out of a single piece, but a few pieces bent and put together to match the curve of the trunk and everything.  When you are done, make sure you use a spray on, rubberized undercoating on the inside and the outside.  This will help alot to keep it from rusting again.  I would recommend the 3M brand undercoating.<P>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mope||02-25-2001||10:52 PM||||i was planning on welding. I like welding and i am pretty damn good at it for only being 17.<P><P>------------------<BR>=======================<P>-= Silver 86 GT, being restored, and following major things to be done: Mr. Mike's Leather, new steering wheel, paint repair, ebrake repair, take apart and clean everything! <A HREF="http://www.mastergraphics.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mope.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mope.cjb.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||02-26-2001||10:42 AM||||me too, to both of those things!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Arc or MIG?  If you can, email me some pics of how bad it is.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mope||02-26-2001||01:29 PM||||arc or mig or gas, i have done them all but prefer mig. i still wanna try aluminum and a tig. we'll see about that though. <P>the rust is pretty bad, i can fit my fist in the hole, that is just the rot through. the hole will probly be big enough for a basketball once i start to cut at it. I will try to take pictures of it but i never seem to remember my camera.<P>Does anyone think i should just cut out the old rust then make the repair with fiberglass matting??<P>lemme know<P>m0pe<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||mope||02-27-2001||07:25 PM||||anyone else?||||reg||5
Z||000006||Jake_Dragon||02-27-2001||07:56 PM||||Mig welding will be your best bet, Tig would work as well but Mig is easier to use in a tight space like the trunk. Welding the outside would be best and keep out moisture better.<BR>If you do decide to use glass pop rivet or tack weld a metal plate in the hole for reinforcement.  <BR>Paint and undercoat will help prevent it from happening again.<BR>Good luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jake_Dragon<BR>1985 2.5L Sport Coupe<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
